(1741890, 235934, 15711, '<td valign="top">I liked this the minute I saw it. It could also serve in the "Thinking of You," "Get Well," and even the "Sympathy" catetgory.  My only complaint is the 2nd flower to the right.  I think the pink of it''s center is a tad distracting.  I think if it were me, I''d clone it out so you are only looking at a single blossom. BUT having said that, to truly denote the duality of two people married, I would have liked to see two complete  blossoms overlapping as the "two become one" type idea for marriage.  The lighting is exquisite and the frame really works well with the color pallette of the shot. Well done.  8</td>', 'I liked this the minute I saw it. It could also serve in the "Thinking of You," "Get Well," and even the "Sympathy" catetgory.  My only complaint is the 2nd flower to the right.  I think the pink of it''s center is a tad distracting.  I think if it were me, I''d clone it out so you are only looking at a single blossom. BUT having said that, to truly denote the duality of two people married, I would have liked to see two complete  blossoms overlapping as the "two become one" type idea for marriage.  The lighting is exquisite and the frame really works well with the color pallette of the shot. Well done.  8', '2005-09-27 09:29:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741894, 236253, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is super imaginative and I like it VERY much.  My main complaint would be all of the "props." The Green Day album, pen, portable phone, etc don''t really add to the shot.  I mean, they probably refer to the person specifically that you miss, but for the general buying public, I think no props at all, other than maybe something that denotes missing a person on a more generic level. Does that make sense?  Since all of the words are kind of busy and your eye is reading them, maybe no belt on the jeans too.  It might be kind of schmaltzy, but maybe holding an empty Valentine candy box, or a picture frame turned away from the viewer, so you just see the back of it.  Just me rambling and thinking out loud here.  The shadows and ligh tare excellent.  The placement of the figure''s torso to the far left works well too, Without all of the props, there would be more negative space, which would give it more of a lonely feeling in my opnion.  Have her laying on grass instead of the rug too like she''s outside day dreaming of the person she is missing.  Hope all of this is helpful.  You certainly have a great eye for detail and the composition is good - just maybe a few less things would work for me.  GOOD LUCK 7</td>', 'This is super imaginative and I like it VERY much.  My main complaint would be all of the "props." The Green Day album, pen, portable phone, etc don''t really add to the shot.  I mean, they probably refer to the person specifically that you miss, but for the general buying public, I think no props at all, other than maybe something that denotes missing a person on a more generic level. Does that make sense?  Since all of the words are kind of busy and your eye is reading them, maybe no belt on the jeans too.  It might be kind of schmaltzy, but maybe holding an empty Valentine candy box, or a picture frame turned away from the viewer, so you just see the back of it.  Just me rambling and thinking out loud here.  The shadows and ligh tare excellent.  The placement of the figure''s torso to the far left works well too, Without all of the props, there would be more negative space, which would give it more of a lonely feeling in my opnion.  Have her laying on grass instead of the rug too like she''s outside day dreaming of the person she is missing.  Hope all of this is helpful.  You certainly have a great eye for detail and the composition is good - just maybe a few less things would work for me.  GOOD LUCK 7', '2005-09-27 09:36:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741899, 236056, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is lovely and perfect for the category.  The dark muted colors are beautiful but do certainly denote the sad sense of the card. The long shadows help add to that as well.  The misty/soft filter works with an ethereal "another world" sense.  Quite striking. I''d love the photograph anyway, whethere this were the challenge or not. That blown out light in the upper right is a tad distracting, but overall quite nicely done. 8</td>', 'This is lovely and perfect for the category.  The dark muted colors are beautiful but do certainly denote the sad sense of the card. The long shadows help add to that as well.  The misty/soft filter works with an ethereal "another world" sense.  Quite striking. I''d love the photograph anyway, whethere this were the challenge or not. That blown out light in the upper right is a tad distracting, but overall quite nicely done. 8', '2005-09-27 09:40:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741907, 233958, 15711, '<td valign="top">I liked this the minute it popped up on my screen.  The monochromatic theme is very effective with the petals blending slowly into the light.  Perfect for the category you chose.  There is enough detail for it to work, but it has a softness that I like. The DOF is good.The light to the left and upper area might be a tad bright, but no demerits for that as it could just be my monitor. With a light colored flower, you have to have a lighter level somewhere anyway.  This would be pretty even if it weren''t for a challenge as specific as this.</td>', 'I liked this the minute it popped up on my screen.  The monochromatic theme is very effective with the petals blending slowly into the light.  Perfect for the category you chose.  There is enough detail for it to work, but it has a softness that I like. The DOF is good.The light to the left and upper area might be a tad bright, but no demerits for that as it could just be my monitor. With a light colored flower, you have to have a lighter level somewhere anyway.  This would be pretty even if it weren''t for a challenge as specific as this.', '2005-09-27 09:48:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741909, 235412, 15711, '<td valign="top">Really perfect for the challenge. It gives that wanderlust sense of "let''s go somewhere." I like the glistening water and the blue tones of the sky and the water. The end of the day sense helps create a peaceful mood. Nicely composed and naturally framed with the boughs of the trees. 8</td>', 'Really perfect for the challenge. It gives that wanderlust sense of "let''s go somewhere." I like the glistening water and the blue tones of the sky and the water. The end of the day sense helps create a peaceful mood. Nicely composed and naturally framed with the boughs of the trees. 8', '2005-09-27 09:49:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741910, 235409, 39768, '<td valign="top">This is so funny; when my father retired (my mother won''t let him smoke in the house) he would drive his pick-up down to the Interstate (I35 in Austin, TX) and sit on a lawnchair in the bed of the truck, smoking cigars and counting Surburbans with a clicker. He even has a bushy grey beard like this.</td>', 'This is so funny; when my father retired (my mother won''t let him smoke in the house) he would drive his pick-up down to the Interstate (I35 in Austin, TX) and sit on a lawnchair in the bed of the truck, smoking cigars and counting Surburbans with a clicker. He even has a bushy grey beard like this.', '2005-09-27 09:49:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741915, 235519, 15711, '<td valign="top">This image is a hoot.  I think the category title is a bit specific, as I thought we were supposed to use a general category, but no biggie.  The shot is wonderful. I love the detail of his woolly coat. The light helps highlight that and the "in your face" sense is hilarious. I think "Hi" or "What''s New?" Might''ve worked better, but that''s just me. In a perfect set up, the other sheep wouldn''t have been behind him, but in the setting, I''m sure that''s not possible.  Really fun and imaginative.</td>', 'This image is a hoot.  I think the category title is a bit specific, as I thought we were supposed to use a general category, but no biggie.  The shot is wonderful. I love the detail of his woolly coat. The light helps highlight that and the "in your face" sense is hilarious. I think "Hi" or "What''s New?" Might''ve worked better, but that''s just me. In a perfect set up, the other sheep wouldn''t have been behind him, but in the setting, I''m sure that''s not possible.  Really fun and imaginative.', '2005-09-27 09:52:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741920, 235487, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is lovely.  The whole scene has a velvety feel to it and yet it''s tack sharp. The green tones with a touch of blue here and there is just wonderful. I like that you are down on the level of the rocks, so that the water is coming right "over you." The composition is done so well and the natural frame of the trees is perfect.  Really nicely done.</td>', 'This is lovely.  The whole scene has a velvety feel to it and yet it''s tack sharp. The green tones with a touch of blue here and there is just wonderful. I like that you are down on the level of the rocks, so that the water is coming right "over you." The composition is done so well and the natural frame of the trees is perfect.  Really nicely done.', '2005-09-27 09:53:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741925, 236285, 15711, '<td valign="top">I see lots of flowers against a black background, but these two gerbera daisies really stand out to me.  I think the orange frame helps this along with the same color orange. This is tack sharp and the composition is spot on. I love the single stem pushing up and out to give the eye an line to follow in the shot. Great lighting too.   This could also work for anniversary as it is two blooms! One of my favorites.</td>', 'I see lots of flowers against a black background, but these two gerbera daisies really stand out to me.  I think the orange frame helps this along with the same color orange. This is tack sharp and the composition is spot on. I love the single stem pushing up and out to give the eye an line to follow in the shot. Great lighting too.   This could also work for anniversary as it is two blooms! One of my favorites.', '2005-09-27 09:55:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741927, 235972, 15711, '<td valign="top">I love the overall tonality of this. The kids playing is perfect for the category you chose. . The leading line sends your eye through the shot. Nicely done.</td>', 'I love the overall tonality of this. The kids playing is perfect for the category you chose. . The leading line sends your eye through the shot. Nicely done.', '2005-09-27 09:57:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741930, 236365, 15711, '<td valign="top">If you ever read my comments, you''ll know I adore bicycles and this is certainly one of them.  The subtle tones and the guys'' shirt being the same as the water really works.  I love the stopped movement. Perfect for the category you chose.  Really nicely done.  He''s looking off into the sea, thinking of the person he misses.  GOOD JOB</td>', 'If you ever read my comments, you''ll know I adore bicycles and this is certainly one of them.  The subtle tones and the guys'' shirt being the same as the water really works.  I love the stopped movement. Perfect for the category you chose.  Really nicely done.  He''s looking off into the sea, thinking of the person he misses.  GOOD JOB', '2005-09-27 10:00:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741932, 234425, 15711, '<td valign="top">Interresting DOF.  The single light part of the rose is a nice touch. I like the overal dark tone of it. This could work for anniversary, birthday, just general as well.   I usually don''t like centered subject matter, but this one seems to work.</td>', 'Interresting DOF.  The single light part of the rose is a nice touch. I like the overal dark tone of it. This could work for anniversary, birthday, just general as well.   I usually don''t like centered subject matter, but this one seems to work.', '2005-09-27 10:02:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741935, 236074, 15711, '<td valign="top">Very cute.  The red lips really make the shot. I like the graininess of it - with the old timey looking I LOVE YOU figure.  Very cute.</td>', 'Very cute.  The red lips really make the shot. I like the graininess of it - with the old timey looking I LOVE YOU figure.  Very cute.', '2005-09-27 10:02:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741945, 236220, 15711, '<td valign="top">Great detailing in the kitty''s eyes.  Very well done with the close up. I like his gaze- just like he''s thinking of someone far away.  The whiskers are tack sharp as is the rest of the facial features.  All animals - extra point. hee hee 8</td>', 'Great detailing in the kitty''s eyes.  Very well done with the close up. I like his gaze- just like he''s thinking of someone far away.  The whiskers are tack sharp as is the rest of the facial features.  All animals - extra point. hee hee 8', '2005-09-27 10:11:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741949, 236300, 15711, '<td valign="top">ROFL.  So glad to see another funny birthday one. Mine is getting lambasted but at least your guy is blowing out candles.  This is really funny and almost looks like it was taken in the 60''s. I love the glasses. The lighting and shadow isn''t "good photography" particularly, but works for this whimsical shot.   Really fun. Thanks for the chuckle.  7</td>', 'ROFL.  So glad to see another funny birthday one. Mine is getting lambasted but at least your guy is blowing out candles.  This is really funny and almost looks like it was taken in the 60''s. I love the glasses. The lighting and shadow isn''t "good photography" particularly, but works for this whimsical shot.   Really fun. Thanks for the chuckle.  7', '2005-09-27 10:13:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741950, 236346, 15711, '<td valign="top">Clever - this stood out amidst the thumbnails.  I like the light and shadow. Good use of filtration. After 2nd review, I''m upping the score.  The more I look at it, the better I like it. A+ for imagination.</td>', 'Clever - this stood out amidst the thumbnails.  I like the light and shadow. Good use of filtration. After 2nd review, I''m upping the score.  The more I look at it, the better I like it. A+ for imagination.', '2005-09-27 10:14:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741956, 236128, 15711, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. It seems almost a tad oversharp to me.  Maybe it''s my monitor. I like the contrast of the hot pink and the green. Maybe a bit more negative space would have worked. I might''ve cloned out the leaf in the lower right and that would have given that extra bit of background. The lighting is good and helps to detail all of the different  areas of the blossom and highlight the variation in color of the petals.</td>', 'Very pretty. It seems almost a tad oversharp to me.  Maybe it''s my monitor. I like the contrast of the hot pink and the green. Maybe a bit more negative space would have worked. I might''ve cloned out the leaf in the lower right and that would have given that extra bit of background. The lighting is good and helps to detail all of the different  areas of the blossom and highlight the variation in color of the petals.', '2005-09-27 10:19:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741959, 236331, 15711, '<td valign="top">I like the glass gems in the cupcake paper.  Different and adds great sparkle to the shot.  I would straighten it though, it''s leaning slightly to the left - just make it parallel with the bottom line of the photo. The green and red are great contrasts as they are opposites on the color wheel. I like the shadow of the scalloped edge in the foreground.</td>', 'I like the glass gems in the cupcake paper.  Different and adds great sparkle to the shot.  I would straighten it though, it''s leaning slightly to the left - just make it parallel with the bottom line of the photo. The green and red are great contrasts as they are opposites on the color wheel. I like the shadow of the scalloped edge in the foreground.', '2005-09-27 10:21:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741960, 236173, 15711, '<td valign="top">HEE HEE HEE!  This makes me smile. The focus is spot on.  I don''t like the line in the lower left, although that''s showing that he is on the road. Maybe from a different angle with more of it showing would have worked for me. I am not crazy about the desat of green - maybe an entire shot done in black and white would''ve worked better for me. There is certainly enough contrast to do this effectively. Still a fun shot and good choice of category. 7</td>', 'HEE HEE HEE!  This makes me smile. The focus is spot on.  I don''t like the line in the lower left, although that''s showing that he is on the road. Maybe from a different angle with more of it showing would have worked for me. I am not crazy about the desat of green - maybe an entire shot done in black and white would''ve worked better for me. There is certainly enough contrast to do this effectively. Still a fun shot and good choice of category. 7', '2005-09-27 10:22:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741961, 235022, 15711, '<td valign="top">Clever and I can see this as a card. I think the title is too long but I''m just one who hates long titles.  I think "Tying the Knot" would have sufficed.  Good lighting and the hairy detail of the rope is great.  Not overly interesting, but it certainly works for the category.</td>', 'Clever and I can see this as a card. I think the title is too long but I''m just one who hates long titles.  I think "Tying the Knot" would have sufficed.  Good lighting and the hairy detail of the rope is great.  Not overly interesting, but it certainly works for the category.', '2005-09-27 10:24:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741964, 235358, 327, '<td valign="top">made me laugh!!!</td>', 'made me laugh!!!', '2005-09-27 10:28:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741967, 235997, 327, '<td valign="top">LOL what a hoot!! Cracked me up!!!!!!!!!!!!!! 9</td>', 'LOL what a hoot!! Cracked me up!!!!!!!!!!!!!! 9', '2005-09-27 10:29:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741968, 236316, 15711, '<td valign="top">I love the repeated shadows. The blue and yellow works great as they are contrasting colors on the color wheel. I think to denote a death (or to me at least) a single bloom would have worked better.  The shadow lends a sense of both sides of it''s BEING, but with two, I almost want to say this would work great for "Getting Married" or "Anniversary" as the duality makes me think of two instead of one.  Does that makes sense.  The photo itself is awesome. I love the linear quality of it and the details are spot on.  Great focus.</td>', 'I love the repeated shadows. The blue and yellow works great as they are contrasting colors on the color wheel. I think to denote a death (or to me at least) a single bloom would have worked better.  The shadow lends a sense of both sides of it''s BEING, but with two, I almost want to say this would work great for "Getting Married" or "Anniversary" as the duality makes me think of two instead of one.  Does that makes sense.  The photo itself is awesome. I love the linear quality of it and the details are spot on.  Great focus.', '2005-09-27 10:30:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741969, 235875, 15711, '<td valign="top">Perfect for the category I love the sun''s reflection coming right to the boat.  Great silhouette.   The golden tones are warm and friendly.  Good choice.</td>', 'Perfect for the category I love the sun''s reflection coming right to the boat.  Great silhouette.   The golden tones are warm and friendly.  Good choice.', '2005-09-27 10:31:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1741972, 235911, 15711, '<td valign="top">This seems a tad out of focus to me. I think a single blossom would denote the sense of a loss better than two. I''d clone out the bug as it doesn''t realy lend itself to the category you chose. I like the idea of the fully opened blossom - like it''s served it''s time here on earth.</td>', 'This seems a tad out of focus to me. I think a single blossom would denote the sense of a loss better than two. I''d clone out the bug as it doesn''t realy lend itself to the category you chose. I like the idea of the fully opened blossom - like it''s served it''s time here on earth.', '2005-09-27 10:33:47.000000', NULL, 1),
