(1765590, 236289, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This is a great greeting card for the "Thinking of You" section. The colors are really nice. The border is rather large but considering the theme, Greeting Cards I find it acceptable. Borders that larger are very common with greeting cards. I like the flower in the top right hand corner. It looks very nice there. I don''t think that you should have been voted down for the border for this shot, and I think that is what happened. Another reason why you might have rec avg scores for this entry is because of the lack of focus. I guess you used a macro setting for this shot? Great mode to use, but it resulted in only a small portion of the flower being in focus. The background needs to be blurred, but not the flower petals, since it is the flower that is the main subject of the photo. Maybe not everybodies cup of tea, but I liked this entry. Good Luck in future challenges!!<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* This is a great greeting card for the "Thinking of You" section. The colors are really nice. The border is rather large but considering the theme, Greeting Cards I find it acceptable. Borders that larger are very common with greeting cards. I like the flower in the top right hand corner. It looks very nice there. I don''t think that you should have been voted down for the border for this shot, and I think that is what happened. Another reason why you might have rec avg scores for this entry is because of the lack of focus. I guess you used a macro setting for this shot? Great mode to use, but it resulted in only a small portion of the flower being in focus. The background needs to be blurred, but not the flower petals, since it is the flower that is the main subject of the photo. Maybe not everybodies cup of tea, but I liked this entry. Good Luck in future challenges!! Mandy', '2005-10-06 18:09:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1765619, 236163, 37779, '<td valign="top">This is quite underrated! This is PERFECT for a card! Wonderful work AS ALWAYS!</td>', 'This is quite underrated! This is PERFECT for a card! Wonderful work AS ALWAYS!', '2005-10-06 18:19:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1765655, 235634, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I remember looking at this photo during the challenge and thinking in my head, "MAN! If the sky wasn''t so blown out this would be great!" Your whole setup is really appealing. The bench in the corner, the leaves from the trees framing the top of the photo, and a water relection. <br/> <br/>The empty bench represents a since of absence--hence your title-Missing You. PERFECT SETUP. The problem I see with this photo is the lighting and that is it. Maybe if you shot this at a different time of day, or played with levels and contrast some? The sky needs more interest. If the sky had more punch with maybe some clouds that would be refected in the water that would really be beautiful.<br/> <br/>mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I remember looking at this photo during the challenge and thinking in my head, "MAN! If the sky wasn''t so blown out this would be great!" Your whole setup is really appealing. The bench in the corner, the leaves from the trees framing the top of the photo, and a water relection.  The empty bench represents a since of absence--hence your title-Missing You. PERFECT SETUP. The problem I see with this photo is the lighting and that is it. Maybe if you shot this at a different time of day, or played with levels and contrast some? The sky needs more interest. If the sky had more punch with maybe some clouds that would be refected in the water that would really be beautiful. mandy', '2005-10-06 18:38:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(1765713, 233958, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Well, I have to hand it to you! Congrats on the high score! There were so many flowers in this challenge and what makes your entry stand out is it simplicity. I love the fact that the flower just fades away into the background. It looks so soft, I can almost smell it. Flower pictures can be very boring and predictable. Your image is not. Wonderful job you did here. I would definatly buy this greeting card. This could be used for many different themes. <br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* Well, I have to hand it to you! Congrats on the high score! There were so many flowers in this challenge and what makes your entry stand out is it simplicity. I love the fact that the flower just fades away into the background. It looks so soft, I can almost smell it. Flower pictures can be very boring and predictable. Your image is not. Wonderful job you did here. I would definatly buy this greeting card. This could be used for many different themes.  Mandy', '2005-10-06 19:06:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1765771, 236163, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I like this photo. I enjoy looking at this scene. I think that is important when taking a picture for a greeting card. I like grain too. I think that it can add character to a photo. IMO, grain can create a feeling or mood with a photo that seems boring otherwise. In your photo the little girl (darling BTW), is picking up shells. She is gathering objects maybe for her collection. This action does not say friendship to me or missing you or even thinking of you. Maybe other voters felt the same way and that is what resulted in a 5.4 score. <br/> <br/>Your picture is very cute and different (added grain and desaturation) which sometimes is not liked by the majority voters. This probably wasn''t what they had in mind for a greeting card. It is not easy to appeal to the masses. I have a very hard time myself and have made up my mind to take pictures that appeal to me and me alone. If I do well in a challenge I am thrilled, but if not it is not the end of the world. Overall, I think that this is a cute picture and I hope the best for you. I see a ribbon in the near future. Your work is excellent and it is just a matter of time. <br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I like this photo. I enjoy looking at this scene. I think that is important when taking a picture for a greeting card. I like grain too. I think that it can add character to a photo. IMO, grain can create a feeling or mood with a photo that seems boring otherwise. In your photo the little girl (darling BTW), is picking up shells. She is gathering objects maybe for her collection. This action does not say friendship to me or missing you or even thinking of you. Maybe other voters felt the same way and that is what resulted in a 5.4 score.  Your picture is very cute and different (added grain and desaturation) which sometimes is not liked by the majority voters. This probably wasn''t what they had in mind for a greeting card. It is not easy to appeal to the masses. I have a very hard time myself and have made up my mind to take pictures that appeal to me and me alone. If I do well in a challenge I am thrilled, but if not it is not the end of the world. Overall, I think that this is a cute picture and I hope the best for you. I see a ribbon in the near future. Your work is excellent and it is just a matter of time.  Mandy', '2005-10-06 19:20:22.000000', NULL, 0),
