(1765885, 235281, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Greetings from the Critique Club! Hello my name is Mandy and I will be your critiquer today. <br/> <br/>First I want to point out the good things. Black and White pictures are my favorite! But with this shot, I think that color would have been a better choice. I think that it is nice that all of the ducks are going in the same direction. I like how they move your eye across the photo from one corner to the opposite corner. So your cropping was good. <br/> <br/>Now for the nick pickety stuff. High Key effects are great on SOME pictures. I think that with water photos they make the photo less intersting. Water shots can be so magical with all of the reflections and movement. Why remove that? The ducks seem to be out of focus, but that could have happened with the processing of the high contrast or when you converted to black and white. <br/> <br/>Your subject does not fit your title. Ducks swimming does not say Missing You, IMO. Maybe if there was one duck swimming alone. Maybe if there was a mother duck and her babies behind her with a definate gap between the second to the last baby duck, a missing you theme would have been easier for the viewer to relate to. Or maybe that is just a bunch of hogwash. What do I know? I hope this was helpful and good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* Greetings from the Critique Club! Hello my name is Mandy and I will be your critiquer today.  First I want to point out the good things. Black and White pictures are my favorite! But with this shot, I think that color would have been a better choice. I think that it is nice that all of the ducks are going in the same direction. I like how they move your eye across the photo from one corner to the opposite corner. So your cropping was good.  Now for the nick pickety stuff. High Key effects are great on SOME pictures. I think that with water photos they make the photo less intersting. Water shots can be so magical with all of the reflections and movement. Why remove that? The ducks seem to be out of focus, but that could have happened with the processing of the high contrast or when you converted to black and white.  Your subject does not fit your title. Ducks swimming does not say Missing You, IMO. Maybe if there was one duck swimming alone. Maybe if there was a mother duck and her babies behind her with a definate gap between the second to the last baby duck, a missing you theme would have been easier for the viewer to relate to. Or maybe that is just a bunch of hogwash. What do I know? I hope this was helpful and good luck in future challenges. mandy', '2005-10-06 19:45:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1765924, 236174, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I am not crazy about the pink tones but they work really good with the girls. The idea of friendship is captured very well in this photo. I can remember my friends and I doing the very same thing! Brings back great memories. <br/> <br/>There are just three things that I didn''t really like about the image. One is that both of the girls are cut off mid-back. Two, is that it was shot on a bed. I think that this would have been cuter if they were infront of a mirror or vanity. Three, one little girl is putting on makeup while the other isn''t doing anything. She is not active in the photo. Maybe if you had the girl on the left putting makeup on the other girl it would have been better. Just a few suggestions. I hope they were helpful.<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I am not crazy about the pink tones but they work really good with the girls. The idea of friendship is captured very well in this photo. I can remember my friends and I doing the very same thing! Brings back great memories.  There are just three things that I didn''t really like about the image. One is that both of the girls are cut off mid-back. Two, is that it was shot on a bed. I think that this would have been cuter if they were infront of a mirror or vanity. Three, one little girl is putting on makeup while the other isn''t doing anything. She is not active in the photo. Maybe if you had the girl on the left putting makeup on the other girl it would have been better. Just a few suggestions. I hope they were helpful. Mandy', '2005-10-06 19:55:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1765998, 234374, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I like how the chairs turn to the right and get visually smaller and smaller and smaller. I like the black and white image. I even like the contemporary feel to it. The chairs are very modern and make a statement. Not sure if that statement is "missing you" however. The building in the background is somewhat dissracting. The picture is intersting in b&amp;w but it does give a "cold" feeling. Not a warm and fuzzy miss you kind of vibe, ya know? Not sure if I would buy this card at a shop. Overall, I think that the picture is interesting and different, just maybe not the best choice for this challenge. Good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I like how the chairs turn to the right and get visually smaller and smaller and smaller. I like the black and white image. I even like the contemporary feel to it. The chairs are very modern and make a statement. Not sure if that statement is "missing you" however. The building in the background is somewhat dissracting. The picture is intersting in b&w but it does give a "cold" feeling. Not a warm and fuzzy miss you kind of vibe, ya know? Not sure if I would buy this card at a shop. Overall, I think that the picture is interesting and different, just maybe not the best choice for this challenge. Good luck in future challenges. Mandy', '2005-10-06 20:18:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1766027, 236267, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Nice face! There are only a few suggestions that I have for this photo. One would be about the border. I like white borders on b&amp;w pictures, nice choice. I would have made it plain white and a little thinner. You really need a plain background for this shot. <br/> <br/>You have captured great details in the hair but the face looks almost too smooth. The tongue is not in focus and that is what our eyes are directly drawn to. I have been trying to touch my tongue to my nose while typing this and I can''t do it. I feel so inadequate as a human being now.<br/> <br/>Overall, great choice for the challenge, very funny picture. Sometimes just a few adjustments like background and the small touches can make a HUDGE difference in your score. So keep that in mind and good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Mandy with the short tongue.</td>', '*Critique Club* Nice face! There are only a few suggestions that I have for this photo. One would be about the border. I like white borders on b&w pictures, nice choice. I would have made it plain white and a little thinner. You really need a plain background for this shot.  You have captured great details in the hair but the face looks almost too smooth. The tongue is not in focus and that is what our eyes are directly drawn to. I have been trying to touch my tongue to my nose while typing this and I can''t do it. I feel so inadequate as a human being now. Overall, great choice for the challenge, very funny picture. Sometimes just a few adjustments like background and the small touches can make a HUDGE difference in your score. So keep that in mind and good luck in future challenges. Mandy with the short tongue.', '2005-10-06 20:27:13.000000', NULL, 0),
