(1770180, 236066, 37673, '<td valign="top">Grettings from CC. <br/> <br/>This shot was nicely done. The natural frame composition is very creative and captures the viewer then distributes your eyes evenly throughout the shot. The fact that you missed the eyes entirely I think plays very well on the title. The focus is dramatic yet not too overpowering. Lighting is good . There is only one "hot" spot and that is just left of the sheep. The color and saturations are very good. Would be curious to know of your post processing steps with this shot were?  Very well done congrats.</td>', 'Grettings from CC.  This shot was nicely done. The natural frame composition is very creative and captures the viewer then distributes your eyes evenly throughout the shot. The fact that you missed the eyes entirely I think plays very well on the title. The focus is dramatic yet not too overpowering. Lighting is good . There is only one "hot" spot and that is just left of the sheep. The color and saturations are very good. Would be curious to know of your post processing steps with this shot were?  Very well done congrats.', '2005-10-08 14:47:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1770673, 236027, 15029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>This is a really fun photo. The image is tack sharp, the composition is excelent, and the subject is funny, and has a great expression. Honestly, I don''t really think that I would change anything, with the exception of the border, which isn''t really a problem, but I tend to not like borders. Possibly showing just a tiny bit more above the ears may have been nice, but it is very good as it is.<br/> <br/>Excelent shot.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) This is a really fun photo. The image is tack sharp, the composition is excelent, and the subject is funny, and has a great expression. Honestly, I don''t really think that I would change anything, with the exception of the border, which isn''t really a problem, but I tend to not like borders. Possibly showing just a tiny bit more above the ears may have been nice, but it is very good as it is. Excelent shot.', '2005-10-08 20:47:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1770681, 235027, 15029, '<td valign="top">Greetings form the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>This is really a breathtaking image, and as already stated, the two things that would improve tis the most would be to have made it larger and straightened the horizon. Judging by the camera, a 640x480 shot should have been manageable as long as you didn''t need to crop much. The connection to the challenge is a bit of a stretch, but possibly something like "Greetings form Chicago" or just "Chicago postcard" would have been a better tie-in to the challenge. <br/> <br/>This also may have looked neat croped more like a panorama, but overall not bad.<br/> <br/>In the future, try to submit a larger image if you can. If you need help with the technical aspects of image resizing/post edditing stuff feel free to P.M. me.</td>', 'Greetings form the Critique Club :) This is really a breathtaking image, and as already stated, the two things that would improve tis the most would be to have made it larger and straightened the horizon. Judging by the camera, a 640x480 shot should have been manageable as long as you didn''t need to crop much. The connection to the challenge is a bit of a stretch, but possibly something like "Greetings form Chicago" or just "Chicago postcard" would have been a better tie-in to the challenge.  This also may have looked neat croped more like a panorama, but overall not bad. In the future, try to submit a larger image if you can. If you need help with the technical aspects of image resizing/post edditing stuff feel free to P.M. me.', '2005-10-08 20:56:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1771030, 236049, 37544, '<td valign="top">* Critique Club *<br/> <br/>Great picture! The sepia tones are wonderful. Gives you a nice warm and fuzzy feeling. I really like everything about it so I am sorry I am the one to critique it. If I have to say something, it would be the mothers facial tones. They are a little blown out, but I don''t think that it hurts your photo. Great job and good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>mandy</td>', '* Critique Club * Great picture! The sepia tones are wonderful. Gives you a nice warm and fuzzy feeling. I really like everything about it so I am sorry I am the one to critique it. If I have to say something, it would be the mothers facial tones. They are a little blown out, but I don''t think that it hurts your photo. Great job and good luck in future challenges. mandy', '2005-10-09 00:47:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1771046, 236251, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I am so jealous! I wish I had your lens!! I am getting a camera like yours though! Anyway...enough about me and my envy. <br/> <br/>The details are amazing and I like the tones too. Needs more negative space. The square crop doesn''t help the image at all. The one major reason this picture did not get a high score from me was because it is a moon. I love the title, very cute and funny. I bet you have a great sense of humor. But, I just don''t think that I would purchase a card for a couple with a moon on it unless they were scientist or something to that nature. <br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* I am so jealous! I wish I had your lens!! I am getting a camera like yours though! Anyway...enough about me and my envy.  The details are amazing and I like the tones too. Needs more negative space. The square crop doesn''t help the image at all. The one major reason this picture did not get a high score from me was because it is a moon. I love the title, very cute and funny. I bet you have a great sense of humor. But, I just don''t think that I would purchase a card for a couple with a moon on it unless they were scientist or something to that nature.  Mandy', '2005-10-09 00:57:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1771061, 235022, 37544, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>The details are wonderful. The composition is good. The rope idea is creative but it doesn''t say wedding to me. Maybe if you would have had a pretty rope (not an old worn out one) tied in a knot with the bride and groom holding the ends. Not like tug of war or anything. Gently holding the rope together showing the wedding bands on the fingers. I think that if it was more "wedding" looking it would have done better.<br/>Good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Mandy</td>', '*Critique Club* The details are wonderful. The composition is good. The rope idea is creative but it doesn''t say wedding to me. Maybe if you would have had a pretty rope (not an old worn out one) tied in a knot with the bride and groom holding the ends. Not like tug of war or anything. Gently holding the rope together showing the wedding bands on the fingers. I think that if it was more "wedding" looking it would have done better.Good luck in future challenges. Mandy', '2005-10-09 01:05:33.000000', NULL, 0),
